{"step_index":565,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T21:02:18Z","content":"# 🌟 Full LeetCode-Style Coding Environment Implemented\n\nWe have upgraded CodeDuel into an authentic **LeetCode-style multi-tab coding environment** with real problem descriptions, collapsible hints, official editorials, reference solutions, and dual testcase inspectors.\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 What Was Built & Upgraded\n\n### 1. Authentic LeetCode Problem Statements & Seeder\n- **Real LeetCode Problem Statements**: Replaced synthetic generator text with authentic LeetCode problem descriptions, examples, exact constraints, and real-world story scenarios (e.g. *Two Sum*, *Contains Duplicate*, *Valid Anagram*, *3Sum*, *Container With Most Water*, *Best Time to Buy and Sell Stock*, *Longest Substring Without Repeating Characters*, *Binary Search*, *Climbing Stairs*, *Number of Islands*, etc.).\n- **Clean LeetCode-Style Method Signatures**: Only the class/function signatures with empty return/`pass` are provided (e.g. `public int[] solve(int[] nums, int target)` in Java, `def solve(self, nums: list[int], target: int) -> list[int]:` in Python).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Multi-Tab Problem Explorer (Left Panel)\nThe problem explorer now has 4 dedicated LeetCode-style tabs:\n- 📑 **`Description`**: Full formatted problem text, topic chips, complexity goals, examples with inputs, outputs, explanations, and constraint badges.\n- 📖 **`Editorial`**: Complete official editorial with Problem Overview, Intuition, Approach 1 (Brute Force $O(n^2)$), Approach 2 (One-Pass Hash Table $O(n)$), and step-by-step Complexity Analysis.\n- 💬 **`Solutions`**: Clean, syntax-highlighted reference solution implementations in **Python 3** and **Java**.\n- 💡 **`Hints`**: Progressive interactive hints accordion — click to reveal **Hint 1**, **Hint 2**, and **Hint 3** as needed!\n\n---\n\n### 3. Dual-Tab Testcase & Result Inspector (Bottom Panel)\n- 🧪 **`Testcase` Tab**: Switch between **Case 1**, **Case 2**, and **Case 3** to inspect the input parameters.\n- 📊 **`Test Result` Tab**: Displays execution verdict (`ACCEPTED` / `WRONG_ANSWER`), exact runtime in ms, memory utilization in MB, efficiency score, and a side-by-side diff comparing **Actual Output** vs **Expected Output**.\n\n---\n\n### 🔄 To Experience the New Environment:\n1. In your backend terminal, restart Spring Boot:\n   - Press **`Ctrl + C`**\n   - Run:\n     ```powershell\n     mvn spring-boot:run\n     ```\n2. Refresh your browser at [`http://localhost:5173/`](http://localhost:5173/).\n3. Open any problem in **Practice Mode** or jump into a **1v1 Versus Arena duel** — you will have the full multi-tab LeetCode experience with Descriptions, Hints, Editorials, and Solutions!"}
